That is impossible from here.	在這裡辦不到那件事。
There may have been a bowl here at one time, but it is not here now!	這裡曾經有過一個碗，但現在已經不在了！
Oh No!  That's such a dangerous river... the current is too strong... you won't be able to escape!	糟了！這是條危險的河流……水流太強……你逃不掉的！
The bank is dangerously steep;  there are safer ways to  reach water.	河岸陡峭危險；還有更安全的方法可以取水。
This is a Raging River filled with boulders and rapids.	這是怒河，河中滿是巨石與急流。
You carefully fill the bucket at the river's edge.	你小心翼翼地在河邊把水桶裝滿。
You drink deeply of the cold river water.	你大口暢飲冰冷的河水。
You are not close enough to the Raging River.	你離怒河不夠近。
Your swimming attempt proved fatal!  The raging current drags you under....	你這次游泳嘗試要了你的命！洶湧的水流把你拖入水底……
The river is dangerous and powerful.  There is a delta of pebbles on its edge.	這條河既危險又湍急，岸邊有一片鵝卵石灘。
As you fill the bucket, the river almost rips it from your grasp.	你裝水時，河水幾乎把水桶從你手中扯走。
The pebbles are round and smooth.	這些鵝卵石又圓又光滑。
You must venture closer to the river.	你得再靠近河流一些。
The only pebbles worth getting are already gone.	值得撿的鵝卵石都已經被拿走了。
From here it looks like an ordinary delta of pebbles.	從這裡看，這只是一片普通的鵝卵石灘。
Your swimming attempt proved fatal!  The raging current drags you under... you are lost....	你這次游泳嘗試要了你的命！洶湧的水流把你拖入水底……你就此消逝……
There are many smooth pebbles next to the river.	河邊有許多光滑圓潤的鵝卵石。
There is a small dwarf close by.  It would be a good idea to be careful.	附近有個小矮人，你最好小心一點。
That little dwarf caught you by surprise.  Is your treasure still OK?	那個小矮人偷襲了你一下，你的寶物還在嗎？
The quick, little dwarf came by to see what you had -- nothing interested him.	動作靈巧的小矮人湊過來看看你身上有什麼——結果什麼都沒引起他的興趣。
Dwarfs are quick, little guys who will try to take your treasure.	矮人們動作靈巧、身形嬌小，總想搶走你的寶物。
He's too quick for you to catch.	他的動作太快，你根本抓不到。
No time to talk to him.  He's in too much of a hurry!	沒時間跟他說話，他趕著要走呢！
The dwarf sees the goat and decides to leave.	矮人看見山羊，決定離開。
Being invisible has protected you from the dwarf.	隱形保護了你和你的寶物，沒讓矮人得逞。
When looking in this small hole, you see a faint green glow.	你往這個小洞裡望去，看見一絲微弱的綠光。
Very cautiously, you reach into the hole, and to your dismay, find nothing.	你小心翼翼地把手伸進洞裡，卻讓你失望的是，裡頭什麼也沒有。
From here it looks like a typical, large rock.	從這裡看，這只是一塊普通的大石頭。
There are several pretty trees in the area and a few rocks.  One rock has a small hole in its base.	這一帶有幾棵漂亮的樹木和幾塊岩石，其中一塊岩石的底部有個小洞。
You feel a stretching sensation... Oh, you're back to your original size.  You can't get out of the small  cave!	你感覺到一陣拉伸感……啊，你恢復原本的大小了。你沒辦法從這個小洞穴裡出去！
One rock has a small hole in its base.	有塊岩石的底部有個小洞。
You notice a hole in the base of a large moss covered rock.	你注意到一塊布滿青苔的大岩石底部有個洞。
The bucket fills with the somewhat swampy water.	水桶裝滿了帶點沼澤氣息的水。
In your thirst, even swamp water is satisfying.	你渴得厲害，就連沼澤水喝起來都很滿足。
This lake looks refreshing, but a little swampy.	這座湖看起來清涼宜人，但帶點沼澤氣息。
This is a very interesting tree, growing in the middle of the lake.	這棵樹長在湖中央，十分有意思。
What a pretty bed of wild flowers.	好一片美麗的野花花圃。
It would be a shame to pick the lovely wild flowers.	摘下這些可愛的野花實在太可惜了。
As you approach the bridge, a mean, ugly troll appears and refuses to let you cross his bridge.	你走近橋邊，一隻凶惡醜陋的矮精靈突然出現，不准你踏上他的橋。
Caution and steep banks advise against getting water here.	河岸陡峭危險，最好別在這裡取水。
You are too far from the river.	你離河流太遠了。
The wooden bridge is old and weather beaten.	這座木橋又老又飽經風霜。
The stream may not be safe to cross.	這條溪流可能不太安全，不宜涉水而過。
Do you really think you can do that?	你真的以為自己做得到嗎？
Fortunately for you, you have no way to do that.	算你走運，你根本沒辦法這麼做。
You throw the dagger and the quick old troll catches it.	你擲出短刀，動作敏捷的老矮精靈一把接住。
You push the troll as hard as you can; he won't budge.	你使盡全力推那隻矮精靈，他卻紋風不動。
Trools have no sympathy.	矮精靈可沒有同情心。
There may be something trollish around, but you're not close enough to do anything about it.	附近或許有什麼與矮精靈有關的東西，但你離得不夠近，做不了什麼。
You throw the dagger and it lands in the stream, lost forever.	你擲出短刀，短刀落入溪流，永遠消失了。
I don't see a troll.	你沒看見矮精靈。
Is there a troll?	這裡有矮精靈嗎？
To what?	給什麼？
What precious treasure would you like to give to the  old troll?	你想把哪件珍貴的寶物送給那隻老矮精靈？
If you don't have it, how can you give it to the troll?	你身上沒有它，要怎麼交給那隻矮精靈？
The troll grabs the treasure and vanishes.	矮精靈抓起寶物，瞬間消失無蹤。
It seems to me that by now you would have learned to be more careful.  You are stuck in the mud at the bottom of this river and sinking fast.	看來事到如今，你早該學乖、更加小心才是。你陷進河底的泥沼裡，正迅速下沉。
You see a crotchety old gnome pacing around his lean-to.	你看見一個脾氣古怪的老侏儒矮人，正在他的窩棚附近踱步。
That is very close but not quite right!	非常接近了，但還不完全正確！
You have the right idea, but your thinking is just a little bit off.	你的想法沒錯，只是差了那麼一點點。
That's right!!!  You've guessed it!!  Here are some magic beans for your outstanding accomplishment!	答對了！！！你猜中了！！這是給你的魔豆，獎勵你這番出色的成就！
The old gnome tells you he has something that may be very useful to you.  Your task is to guess his name in three guesses and his gift will be yours.  Good luck!  What is your first guess?	老侏儒矮人告訴你，他有樣東西也許對你很有用。你的任務是在三次機會內猜中他的名字，猜中禮物就是你的。祝你好運！你的第一個猜測是什麼？
You still haven't guessed my name!	你還沒猜中我的名字呢！
The gnome is old and bent under the weight of years, but a playful wisdom still brightens his eyes.	這個侏儒矮人年事已高、被歲月壓彎了腰，但眼中仍閃著一絲頑皮的智慧光芒。
They look like beans.  Interesting.	看起來像豆子，真有意思。
It is a heavy, gold, skeleton key.	這是一把沉甸甸的萬能金鑰匙。
It would be unwise to kill a gnome.	殺害侏儒矮人可不是明智之舉。
Being careful that you get every one of them, you place the beans in your pocket.	你小心翼翼地一顆不漏，把豆子全放進口袋裡。
It is heavy and cold.	它又沉又冰冷。
The gnome can't hear you from there.	你站在那裡，侏儒矮人聽不見你說話！
You should get a little closer.	你應該再靠近一點。
There are no beans here.	這裡沒有豆子。
The key to your problems is elsewhere.	能解決你問題的鑰匙不在這裡。
There is no gnome here.	這裡沒有侏儒矮人。
That's too far away.	那太遠了。
Where did you get that idea?  That's not even close!	你這想法是打哪來的？差得遠呢！
You know that's not right!	你自己也知道那不對！
What is your next guess?	你的下一個猜測是什麼？
You didn't guess the gnome's name, but he left you a gold key anyway.  Better luck next time!	你沒猜中侏儒矮人的名字，但他還是留了一把金鑰匙給你。祝你下次好運！
There is no place to safely get a drink.	這裡沒有能安全喝水的地方。
There is no place to safely get water.	這裡沒有能安全取水的地方。
You slip down the bank into the river far below.  Your cries for help are not heard.	你從河岸滑落，跌進下方遙遠的河水裡。你的呼救聲沒人聽見。
The gnome's lean-to doesn't look very sturdy.	侏儒矮人的窩棚看起來不太堅固。
As you approach the bridge, a mean, ugly troll appears.  He will not let you cross his bridge.	你走近橋邊，一隻凶惡醜陋的矮精靈出現了。他不准你踏上他的橋。
The old goat seeing the troll, the archenemy of all goats, charges the troll and butts him into oblivion!  The bridge is now yours.	老山羊一看見矮精靈——山羊們的頭號宿敵——立刻朝他猛衝過去，一頭把他撞得魂飛魄散！這座橋現在是你的了。
This bridge is the only way to cross the river here.	這座橋是這裡唯一能過河的路。
The river runs swiftly between steep banks.	河水在陡峭的兩岸之間湍急流動。
Don't do it!  The bank is steep, muddy, and dangerous.	別這麼做！河岸又陡又泥濘，十分危險。
You can't reach the river from here.	你在這裡搆不到河流。
This troll is big, strong, and mean-looking.  Don't mess with this troll!	這隻矮精靈體型高大、力氣過人，看起來凶惡無比。別去招惹他！
It's just about impossible to kill a troll.	要殺死矮精靈幾乎是不可能的事。
It's lucky you don`t have any way to try that!	算你走運，你根本沒辦法試試看！
He demands a treasure for passage across his bridge.	他要求你獻上寶物，才准你過橋。
The dagger sings through the air... to a perfect catch by the troll.  "Nice dagger, but it ain't no treasure!" he growls.	短刀劃破空氣飛出……穩穩落入矮精靈手中。他咆哮道：「短刀是不錯，可這不算什麼寶物！」
You try very hard to push the ugly troll, but you can't budge him.	你使盡全力推那隻醜陋的矮精靈，卻絲毫推不動他。
Trolls have no sympathy.	矮精靈可沒有同情心。
He isn't there!  Try the bridge.	他不在那裡！去橋上找找看。
You throw the dagger and it falls into the flowing stream.	你擲出短刀，短刀落入流動的溪水中。
Good news: no troll.	好消息：沒有矮精靈。
What priceless treasure are you giving the old troll?	你要把哪件無價的寶物送給那隻老矮精靈？
You don't have any.	你身上沒有。
You would have to throw it from here!	你得從這裡把它丟出去！
Grasping the precious treasure in a dirt-covered paw, the troll disappears under the bridge.	矮精靈用沾滿泥土的爪子抓起珍貴的寶物，消失在橋下。
You have slipped down the muddy bank and lodged in the  river's bed.  Good knight.	你從泥濘的河岸滑落，卡進了河床裡——晚安了，好騎士。
You have fallen in the raging current and are swept under.  I'm afraid your end has come.	你跌進洶湧的水流，被捲入水底。恐怕你的大限已至。
It is an old stone bridge dating to ancient times.	這是一座古老的石橋，年代久遠。
Very carefully, the bucket fills with water from the  rapid river.	你小心翼翼地讓水桶裝滿湍急的河水。
Being careful not to slip in, you drink deeply of the cool water.	你小心不讓自己滑落水中，大口暢飲清涼的河水。
You are too far from the water.	你離水太遠了。
It tastes very refreshing to a thirsty wanderer.	對一個口渴的旅人來說，這滋味十分沁涼解渴。
The crystal clear water fills up the bucket.	清澈見底的水注滿了水桶。
When you look in the doorway, you see a poor, starving woodcutter and his wife.	你朝門口望去，看見一位可憐挨餓的樵夫和他的妻子。
How are you going to use the ax when you can't even get it out of this stump?	你連斧頭都拔不出樹樁，要怎麼用它？
The trees were cut from these stumps long ago.	很久以前，這些樹木就是從這些樹樁上砍下的。
When you look in the window, you see a poor, starving woodcutter and his wife.	你從窗戶望進去，看見一個貧窮挨餓的樵夫和他的妻子。
Watch out!!!  There is an ogre nearby!  He will crush you in his strong arms if he catches you.	小心！！！附近有隻鬼怪！要是被他抓到，他會用強壯的雙臂把你壓碎。
With the magic shield, no harm will come to you.	有了靈盾護身，你不會受到任何傷害。
Fortunately, you are invisible and the ogre can't see you.	幸好你是隱形的，鬼怪看不見你。
The ogre's vision is not keen enough to see you.	鬼怪的視力不夠敏銳，看不見你。
The ogre can see you now!	鬼怪現在看得見你了！
The dagger is of little use against such a mean creature.  I would save it if I were you.	短刀對付這種凶惡的生物沒什麼用。換作是我，會把它留著。
OK.  You drop the dagger.	好，你放下了短刀。
That is a ferocious looking beast.  Please keep your distance!	那是隻看起來凶猛駭人的野獸，請保持距離！
There is no ogre here.	這裡沒有鬼怪。
Ogres are practically indestructible.	鬼怪幾乎是打不死的。
At one time these were very pretty trees.	這些樹木曾經十分漂亮。
Do you really want to try that?	你真的想試試看嗎？
The delightful wild flowers brighten up your day.	這些迷人的野花讓你心情愉快了起來。
Their perfume is joyful, sweet, and light.	它們的香氣輕盈甜美，教人心曠神怡。
Ogres don't talk, they growl!	鬼怪不會說話，只會咆哮！
